# AidingEventReport: generated by tools/generate_interfaces.py from more_generic_models 0.1.0. Do not edit.
# One correction the vehicle's estimator attempted with a reading of an aiding or navigation sensor, issued at the API's sample
# after it is handled: ``sensor`` the kind of the reading, ``accepted`` whether the estimate took it, ``innovation`` the
# innovation vector z - h(x) in the units of the reading's rows (empty where the estimator did not form one), ``nis`` the
# normalised innovation squared (NaN where none was formed) and ``reason`` why it was refused (empty when accepted).
#
# Frames (owner decision): positions NED about the scenario origin (x north, y east), body quantities FRD, angles in rad from
# north clockwise, time in s on the scenario clock.
std_msgs/Header header  # stamp = t rounded to ns; frame_id map_ned for positions
uint64 stream_seq  # publication counter per vehicle across all report types (restores the drain order)
float64 t  # unit: s; the sample instant on the scenario clock, exactly
string sensor
bool accepted
float64[] innovation  # GAP: unit and frame not given by the library
float64 nis  # GAP: unit and frame not given by the library
string reason
